course: dictionary
lesson: 13349
title: Hallowed: holy and deeply respected
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Hallowed is an old word that means holy, or treated with great respect. Look at the words around it to work out the meaning. «The old church is a hallowed place, where people speak in whispers.» People whisper in a church because it is holy and special, so hallowed must mean holy or deeply respected.
explain: Sometimes hallowed means respected because of its past, not because of religion. «The stadium is hallowed ground for football fans.» Great matches and famous players have made it special, so fans treat it with respect.
explain: You may meet hallow as a verb too. In an old prayer, «hallowed be thy name» means may God's name be treated as holy. Halloween is linked to this word, because its name comes from All Hallows' Eve, the night before All Saints' Day.
fact: Hallowed means holy, or treated with great respect.
fact: Hallowed can describe a place with a special history, like a famous stadium or a war cemetery.
fact: Hallow is an old word meaning to make holy or to honour as holy.
fact: «Hallowed be thy name» is from the Lord's Prayer, said in many schools and churches.
fact: Halloween comes from All Hallows' Eve, the eve of All Saints' Day.
exercise: «The stadium is hallowed ground for football fans, after decades of great matches.» What does hallowed mean here? | *Greatly respected because of its history | Very cold | Muddy and wet | Noisy and crowded
exercise: In the Lord's Prayer we say «hallowed be thy name». What does hallowed mean? | Forgotten | Loud | *Holy, treated with great respect
exercise: «The war cemetery is a hallowed place where soldiers rest.» Find and copy the word that means holy or deeply respected. | cemetery | *hallowed | soldiers | rest
test: «Visitors walk quietly through the hallowed church, out of respect.» Why do they walk quietly? | Because the church is closed | *Because the church is holy and treated with great respect | Because they are tired | Because they are looking for a lost coin
test: Halloween gets its name from All Hallows' Eve, the night before which holy day? | Christmas Day | *All Saints' Day | New Year's Day | Easter Sunday
exam: In an old prayer, what does to hallow mean? | Make dirty | Count carefully | *Make holy or honour as holy | Hide away
